# Conventional Commits, checked against scripts/commit-convention.ts - the same
# file `ci-cli` runs against the pull request title.
#
# Be clear about what this can and cannot do. Pull requests here are squashed, and
# the squash takes its subject from the TITLE, which is edited on GitHub long after
# this hook has run. So this does not protect release-please; the `ci-cli` check
# does. What it does is stop you building a habit that the gate will reject, and
# catch the typo while the message is still in your editor.
bun run scripts/commit-convention.ts "$1"
